## Modes

Modes: `careful`, `pair`, `afk`. No mode = default. Details live in `.cursor/skills/run-task-loop/modes/<mode>.md`.

## Switching

- Only the user switches modes. Never switch yourself or suggest a switch.
- A message switches mode only when it names the mode with the word "mode" or the skill: `careful mode`, `mode: pair`, `/run-task-loop afk`. `default mode` or `mode: default` returns to default.
- A bare mode word ("afk", "be careful") is not a switch.
- On a switch, read the mode file now, then follow it.
- The mode applies to this chat only. Do not store it in files.

## Staying in the mode

- Start every reply with `[mode: <name>]`. Omit the tag in default.
- A mode named in your earlier replies or in the conversation summary stays active until the user changes it.
- Re-read the mode file at the start of each new task or phase, and whenever the earlier conversation has been summarized.

## Subagents

- If you are a subagent, ignore this rule: no tag, no mode file. Follow only the prompt you were given.
- When you spawn a subagent, follow the "Subagents" section of the active mode file. In default, add nothing.
- Mode text for a subagent only limits risk or questions. It never changes the subagent's task (for example, never tell a subagent that is writing tests not to write tests).
